WEBVTT


00:00:01.650 --> 00:00:06.540
Take a simple needle arrangement
and racking for a beautiful

00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:08.440
open work lace-like fabric.

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:12.360
The needles out of work
create the open spaces

00:00:16.710 --> 00:00:22.380
With this needle arrangement set
your ribber to H5 and knit two rows

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:27.510
swing to H3 knit to rows and repeat.

00:00:31.505 --> 00:00:35.195
Now here's a tip, since we're
racking every other row, if

00:00:35.195 --> 00:00:38.705
you need to stop knitting end
with the carriage on the left.

00:00:39.425 --> 00:00:42.125
That way you won't forget
if you've racked or not.

00:00:42.635 --> 00:00:46.925
When you come back, you'll knit to
the right and it'll be time to rack.

00:01:03.599 --> 00:01:06.030
I removed my ribber for this sample.

00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:11.070
And because I was in a hurry, this is just
a swatch, I cast on with full needle rib,

00:01:11.220 --> 00:01:15.360
then dropped the stitches and put needles
in and out of work for the pattern.

00:01:16.365 --> 00:01:17.565
Then continued knitting.

00:01:19.725 --> 00:01:21.165
The oops, on the right.

00:01:21.195 --> 00:01:27.315
If I had used a 7 or a wire weight hanger,
this could have prevented the mess.

00:01:28.755 --> 00:01:30.315
I hope you'll try this technique.

00:01:30.495 --> 00:01:34.125
Different needle arrangements,
different racking sequences will create

00:01:34.125 --> 00:01:36.675
completely different lace like fabrics.

